# =============================================================================
# WHITELIST .gitignore  --  deny by default
#
# Line 1 ignores EVERYTHING. Files are then added back one at a time below.
# This is deliberate: a blacklist has to anticipate every secret, and any new
# file dropped into /config would be committed by default. Here a new file is
# invisible to git until someone deliberately un-ignores it, so a token or a
# password cannot land in the repo by accident.
#
# /config holds live secrets: secrets.yaml, .storage/ (auth tokens, refresh
# tokens, OAuth credentials, API keys for every integration), the recorder
# database, Alexa cookies and TTS caches. None of it is whitelisted.
# =============================================================================
*

!.gitignore

# ---- documentation ----------------------------------------------------------
!README.md
!docs/
!docs/**

# ---- core Home Assistant config ---------------------------------------------
# Safe to publish: every credential is a !secret reference, verified by scan.
!configuration.yaml
!automations.yaml
!scripts.yaml
!groups.yaml
!customize.yaml
!known_devices.yaml

# ---- bedside dashboard (iPhone kiosk) ---------------------------------------
!bedside.yaml
!themes/
!themes/bedside/
!themes/bedside/*.yaml

# ---- View Assist custom assets ----------------------------------------------
# Only our own files. The upstream views are managed by the View Assist
# updater and would be overwritten anyway, so they are not tracked.
!view_assist/
!view_assist/views/
!view_assist/views/stocks/
!view_assist/views/stocks/stocks.yaml
!view_assist/views/stocks/chart_home.apex.yaml
!view_assist/views/stocks/chart_home.buttoncard.yaml
!view_assist/views/stocks/chart_home.candles.yaml
!view_assist/dashboard/
!view_assist/dashboard/user_dashboard.yaml

# ---- operational scripts ----------------------------------------------------
!disk_report.sh
!cleanup.sh
!echo_net_watch.sh

# ---- secrets template (placeholder values only) -----------------------------
!secrets.yaml.example

# =============================================================================
# Belt and braces. These are already covered by "*", but restated so that an
# accidental "!" rule above can never expose them.
# =============================================================================
secrets.yaml
.storage/
.cloud/
.ssh/
.cache/
deps/
tts/
www/community/
custom_components/
config_backups/
node-red/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.log
*.log.*
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.pickle
*.cookies
*.token
*.conf
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.pub
id_*
options.xml
zwcfg_*.xml
cameraURLs.txt
go2rtc.yaml
life360.conf
.HA_VERSION
